{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"vinyl-cheesy-termite","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe parent-first cascade is implemented twice: `src/rebar/_commands/claim.py:200-237` (hardcodes the `open` parent via `_resolve_open_parent`) and `src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:421-493` (`_cascade_parent_first`, driven by the `_CASCADING_EDGES` table at `transition.py:414`). The table was added after bug `cranial-sulfur-peafowl` and extended again for `paragonite-fruited-minnow` — both were \"an edge the cascade did not know about\" — and the claim copy still cannot express any edge but `open→in_progress`. The ghost/init preconditions at `transition.py:308-323` and `claim.py:156-169` are byte-identical. Open task `convenient-unrational-songbird` covers the table's one-status-per-edge shape and open bug `despotic-prime-reindeer` covers inbound reconcile bypassing the cascade; this story is the single implementation both of those then build on.\n\n## Approach\nAdd `src/rebar/_commands/lifecycle_cascade.py` with `cascade_parent_first(ticket_id, edge, op, tracker, *, seen, **op_kwargs)` holding the one `_CASCADING_EDGES` table, the TOCTOU re-check, and the error rewrap preserving `ConcurrencyMismatch`; `claim_compute` passes `op=claim_compute` (assignee passthrough kept, `--review` deliberately not propagated per `claim.py:178-183`), `transition_compute` passes itself. Fold the ghost/init triple into `_seam.require_live_ticket`. Guard: `_CASCADING_EDGES` is defined once (AST check, no marker needed).\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_commands/lifecycle_cascade.py` (new), `src/rebar/_commands/claim.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/transition.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py`, `tests/unit/commands/test_lifecycle_cascade.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: claiming a child of an open parent claims the parent first on both surfaces. Edge: a parent already taken by another session raises `ConcurrencyMismatch` with the same exit code as today. Pinning: `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_claim_transition_parent_cascade.py` and the cascade tests from `cranial-sulfur-peafowl`/`paragonite-fruited-minnow` pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `grep -rn \"_CASCADING_EDGES\\s*=\" src/rebar` returns one definition; checked by the grep and the guard test.\n- [ ] Every edge in the table is exercised by the same test for both `claim` and `transition`; checked by a parametrised test over the table.\n- [ ] Pinning suites pass unchanged; checked by `pytest`.\n","id":"4329-4761-6e3d-41d7","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","priority":2,"tags":["consolidation","janitor","fortnight-review"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"One parent-first cascade shared by claim and transition"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787352180718047001,"uuid":"e93eaa61-5ece-49fc-80c6-8e2aa276b256"}